nswer":"Person + と + verb","explanation":"Person + と + action expresses with someone. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-19-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “With a person と”?","options":["今日は暑いです。","猫がいます。","水を飲みます。","友達と映画を見ます。"],"answer":"友達と映画を見ます。","explanation":"友達と映画を見ます。 (Tomodachi to eiga o mimasu.) means “I watch a movie with a friend.”."},{"id":"n5-19-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 友達と映画を見ます。","options":["There is a cat.","I drink water.","I watch a movie with a friend.","It is hot today."],"answer":"I watch a movie with a friend.","explanation":"友達と映画を見ます。 (Tomodachi to eiga o mimasu.) means “I watch a movie with a friend.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":20,"category":"Particles","title":"Complete list と","pattern":"Noun と Noun","meaning":"A and B (complete list)","explanation":"Noun と Noun expresses a and b (complete list). Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Noun A + と + Noun B","difficulty":"Beginner","examples":[{"japanese":"パンと牛乳を買いました。","romaji":"Pan to gyuunyuu o kaimashita.","meaning":"I bought bread and milk."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Noun A + と + Noun B; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-20-meaning","prompt":"What does “Noun と Noun” mean?","options":["A and B (complete list)","Topic of the sentence","Subject / newly identified information","Direct object"],"answer":"A and B (complete list)","explanation":"Noun と Noun expresses a and b (complete list). Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-20-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Complete list と”.","options":["Topic + は + comment","Subject + が + predicate","Object + を + verb","Noun A + と + Noun B"],"answer":"Noun A + と + Noun B","explanation":"Noun と Noun expresses a and b (complete list). Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-20-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Complete list と”?","options":["猫がいます。","水を飲みます。","パンと牛乳を買いました。","今日は暑いです。"],"answer":"パンと牛乳を買いました。","explanation":"パンと牛乳を買いました。 (Pan to gyuunyuu o kaimashita.) means “I bought bread and milk.”."},{"id":"n5-20-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: パンと牛乳を買いました。","options":["I drink water.","I bought bread and milk.","It is hot today.","There is a cat."],"answer":"I bought bread and milk.","explanation":"パンと牛乳を買いました。 (Pan to gyuunyuu o kaimashita.) means “I bought bread and milk.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":21,"category":"Demonstratives","title":"This / that これそれあれ","pattern":"これ / それ / あれ","meaning":"This / that / that over there","explanation":"これ / それ / あれ expresses this / that / that over there. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"これ / それ / あれ + は + noun + です","difficulty":"Beginner","examples":[{"japanese":"これは私の本です。","romaji":"Kore wa watashi no hon desu.","meaning":"This is my book."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction これ / それ / あれ + は + noun + です; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-21-meaning","prompt":"What does “これ / それ / あれ” mean?","options":["A is B","A is not B","A is not B (formal)","This / that / that over there"],"answer":"This / that / that over there","explanation":"これ / それ / あれ expresses this / that / that over there. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-21-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “This / that これそれあれ”.","options":["Noun + は + Noun + じゃありません","Noun + は + Noun + ではありません","これ / それ / あれ + は + noun + です","Noun + は + Noun + です"],"answer":"これ / それ / あれ + は + noun + です","explanation":"これ / それ / あれ expresses this / that / that over there. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-21-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “This / that これそれあれ”?","options":["これは問題ではありません。","これは私の本です。","私は学生です。","私は医者じゃありません。"],"answer":"これは私の本です。","explanation":"これは私の本です。 (Kore wa watashi no hon desu.) means “This is my book.”."},{"id":"n5-21-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: これは私の本です。","options":["This is my book.","I am a student.","I am not a doctor.","This is not a problem."],"answer":"This is my book.","explanation":"これは私の本です。 (Kore wa watashi no hon desu.) means “This is my book.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":22,"category":"Demonstratives","title":"Noun demonstratives このそのあの","pattern":"この / その / あの + noun","meaning":"This / that + noun","explanation":"この / その / あの + noun expresses this / that + noun. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"この / その / あの + noun","difficulty":"Beginner","examples":[{"japanese":"この本は新しいです。","romaji":"Kono hon wa atarashii desu.","meaning":"This book is new."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction この / その / あの + noun; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-22-meaning","prompt":"What does “この / その / あの + noun” mean?","options":["A is not B","A is not B (formal)","This / that + noun","A is B"],"answer":"This / that + noun","explanation":"この / その / あの + noun expresses this / that + noun. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-22-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Noun demonstratives このそのあの”.","options":["Noun + は + Noun + ではありません","この / その / あの + noun","Noun + は + Noun + です","Noun + は + Noun + じゃありません"],"answer":"この / その / あの + noun","explanation":"この / その / あの + noun expresses this / that + noun. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-22-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Noun demonstratives このそのあの”?","options":["この本は新しいです。","私は学生です。","私は医者じゃありません。","これは問題ではありません。"],"answer":"この本は新しいです。","explanation":"この本は新しいです。 (Kono hon wa atarashii desu.) means “This book is new.”."},{"id":"n5-22-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: この本は新しいです。","options":["I am a student.","I am not a doctor.","This is not a problem.","This book is new."],"answer":"This book is new.","explanation":"この本は新しいです。 (Kono hon wa atarashii desu.) means “This book is new.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":23,"category":"Demonstratives","title":"Place words ここそこあそこ","pattern":"ここ / そこ / あそこ","meaning":"Here / there / over there","explanation":"ここ / そこ / あそこ expresses here / there / over there. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"ここ / そこ / あそこ + は / に","difficulty":"Beginner","examples":[{"japanese":"ここは図書館です。","romaji":"Koko wa toshokan desu.","meaning":"This place is a library."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction ここ / そこ / あそこ + は / に; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-23-meaning","prompt":"What does “ここ / そこ / あそこ” mean?","options":["A is not B (formal)","Here / there / over there","A is B","A is not B"],"answer":"Here / there / over there","explanation":"ここ / そこ / あそこ expresses here / there / over there. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-23-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Place words ここそこあそこ”.","options":["ここ / そこ / あそこ + は / に","Noun + は + Noun + です","Noun + は + Noun + じゃありません","Noun + は + Noun + ではありません"],"answer":"ここ / そこ / あそこ + は / に","explanation":"ここ / そこ / あそこ expresses here / there / over there. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-23-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Place words ここそこあそこ”?","options":["私は学生です。","私は医者じゃありません。","これは問題ではありません。","ここは図書館です。"],"answer":"ここは図書館です。","explanation":"ここは図書館です。 (Koko wa toshokan desu.) means “This place is a library.”."},{"id":"n5-23-translation","prompt":"Choose the me