) means “When is your birthday?”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":31,"category":"Questions","title":"How どう","pattern":"どう + predicate","meaning":"How / what is it like","explanation":"どう + predicate expresses how / what is it like. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"どう + ですか / verb","difficulty":"Beginner","examples":[{"japanese":"日本の生活はどうですか。","romaji":"Nihon no seikatsu wa dou desu ka.","meaning":"How is life in Japan?"}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction どう + ですか / verb; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-31-meaning","prompt":"What does “どう + predicate” mean?","options":["What","How / what is it like","Where","Who"],"answer":"How / what is it like","explanation":"どう + predicate expresses how / what is it like. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-31-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “How どう”.","options":["どう + ですか / verb","どこ + ですか / に / で","だれ + が / は + predicate","何 + を / が / ですか"],"answer":"どう + ですか / verb","explanation":"どう + predicate expresses how / what is it like. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-31-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “How どう”?","options":["駅はどこですか。","あの人はだれですか。","これは何ですか。","日本の生活はどうですか。"],"answer":"日本の生活はどうですか。","explanation":"日本の生活はどうですか。 (Nihon no seikatsu wa dou desu ka.) means “How is life in Japan?”."},{"id":"n5-31-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 日本の生活はどうですか。","options":["Who is that person?","What is this?","How is life in Japan?","Where is the station?"],"answer":"How is life in Japan?","explanation":"日本の生活はどうですか。 (Nihon no seikatsu wa dou desu ka.) means “How is life in Japan?”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":32,"category":"Questions","title":"Price いくら","pattern":"いくら + ですか","meaning":"How much","explanation":"いくら + ですか expresses how much. Identify the role