stem + ました","Verb stem + ませんでした"],"answer":"Verb stem + ます","explanation":"Verb stem + ます expresses do / will do politely. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-35-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Polite non-past ます”?","options":["コーヒーを飲みません。","昨日、本を読みました。","昨日は勉強しませんでした。","毎朝パンを食べます。"],"answer":"毎朝パンを食べます。","explanation":"毎朝パンを食べます。 (Maiasa pan o tabemasu.) means “I eat bread every morning.”."},{"id":"n5-35-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 毎朝パンを食べます。","options":["I read a book yesterday.","I did not study yesterday.","I eat bread every morning.","I do not drink coffee."],"answer":"I eat bread every morning.","explanation":"毎朝パンを食べます。 (Maiasa pan o tabemasu.) means “I eat bread every morning.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":36,"category":"Verbs","title":"Polite negative ません","pattern":"Verb stem + ません","meaning":"Do not / will not","explanation":"Verb stem + ません expresses do not / will not. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Verb stem + ません","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"コーヒーを飲みません。","romaji":"Koohii o nomimasen.","meaning":"I do not drink coffee."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Verb stem + ません; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-36-meaning","prompt":"What does “Verb stem + ません” mean?","options":["Do not / will not","Do / will do politely","Did","Did not"],"answer":"Do not / will not","explanation":"Verb stem + ません expresses do not / will not. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-36-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Polite negative ません”.","options":["Verb stem + ます","Verb stem + ました","Verb stem + ませんでした","Verb stem + ません"],"answer":"Verb stem + ません","explanation":"Verb stem + ません expresses do not / will not. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-36-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Polite negative ません”?","options":["昨日、本を読みました。","昨日は勉強しませんでした。","コーヒーを飲みません。","毎朝パンを食べます。"],"answer":"コーヒーを飲みません。","explanation":"コーヒーを飲みません。 (Koohii o nomimasen.) means “I do not drink coffee.”."},{"id":"n5-36-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: コーヒーを飲みません。","options":["I did not study yesterday.","I do not drink coffee.","I eat bread every morning.","I read a book yesterday."],"answer":"I do not drink coffee.","explanation":"コーヒーを飲みません。 (Koohii o nomimasen.) means “I do not drink coffee.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":37,"category":"Verbs","title":"Polite past ました","pattern":"Verb stem + ました","meaning":"Did","explanation":"Verb stem + ました expresses did. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Verb stem + ました","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"昨日、本を読みました。","romaji":"Kinou hon o yomimashita.","meaning":"I read a book yesterday."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Verb stem + ました; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-37-meaning","prompt":"What does “Verb stem + ました” mean?","options":["Do / will do politely","Do not / will not","Did not","Did"],"answer":"Did","explanation":"Verb stem + ました expresses did. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-37-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Polite past ました”.","options":["Verb stem + ません","Verb stem + ませんでした","Verb stem + ました","Verb stem + ます"],"answer":"Verb stem + ました","explanation":"Verb stem + ました expresses did. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-37-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Polite past ました”?","options":["昨日は勉強しませんでした。","昨日、本を読みました。","毎朝パンを食べます。","コーヒーを飲みません。"],"answer":"昨日、本を読みました。","explanation":"昨日、本を読みました。 (Kinou hon o yomimashita.) means “I read a book yesterday.”."},{"id":"n5-37-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 昨日、本を読みました。","options":["I read a book yesterday.","I eat bread every morning.","I do not drink coffee.","I did not study yesterday."],"answer":"I read a book yesterday.","explanation":"昨日、本を読みました。 (Kinou hon o yomimashita.) means “I read a book yesterday.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":38,"category":"Verbs","title":"Past negative ませんでした","pattern":"Verb stem + ませんでした","meaning":"Did not","explanation":"Verb stem + ませんでした expresses did not. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Verb stem + ませんでした","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"昨日は勉強しませんでした。","romaji":"Kinou wa benkyou shimasen deshita.","meaning":"I did not study yesterday."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Verb stem + ませんでした; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-38-meaning","prompt":"What does “Verb stem + ませんでした” mean?","options":["Do not / will not","Did","Did not","Do / will do politely"],"answer":"Did not","explanation":"Verb stem + ませんでした expresses did not. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-38-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Past negative ませんでした”.","options":["Verb stem + ました","Verb stem + ませんでした","Verb stem + ます","Verb stem + ません"],"answer":"Verb stem + ませんでした","explanation":"Verb stem + ませんでした expresses did not. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-38-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Past negative ませんでした”?","options":["昨日は勉強しませんでした。","毎朝パンを食べます。","コーヒーを飲みません。","昨日、本を読みました。"],"answer":"昨日は勉強しませんでした。","explanation":"昨日は勉強しませんでした。 (Kinou wa benkyou shimasen deshita.) means “I did not study yesterday.”."},{"id":"n5-38-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 昨日は勉強しませんでした。","options":["I eat bread every morning.","I do not drink coffee.","I read a book yesterday.","I did not study yesterday."],"answer":"I did not study yesterday.","explanation":"昨日は勉強しませんでした。 (Kinou wa benkyou shimasen deshita.) means “I did not study yesterday.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":39,"category":"Verbs","title":"Dictionary form","pattern":"Plain non-past verb","meaning":"Do / will do (plain)","explanation":"Plain non-past verb expresses do / will do (plain). Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Dictionary verb form","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"毎日走る。","romaji":"Mainichi hashiru.","meaning":"I run every day."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Dictionary verb form; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-39-meaning","prompt":"What does “Plain non-past verb” mean?","options":["Did","Do / will do (plain)","Do / will do politely","Do not / will not"],"answer":"Do / will do (plain)","explanation":"Plain non-past verb expresses do / will do (plain). Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-39-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Dictionary form”.","options":["Dictionary verb form","Verb stem + ます","Verb stem + ません","Verb stem + ました"],"answer":"Dictionary verb form","explanation":"Plain non-past verb expresses do / will do (plain). Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-39-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Dictionary form”?","options":["毎朝パンを食べます。","コーヒーを飲みません。","昨日、本を読みました。","毎日走る。"],"answer":"毎日走る。","explanation":"毎日走る。 (Mainichi hashiru.) means “I run every day.”."},{"id":"n5-39-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 毎日走る。","options":["I do not drink coffee.","I read a book yesterday.","I run every day.","I eat bread every morning."],"answer":"I run every day.","explanation":"毎日走る。 (Mainichi hashiru.) means “I run every day.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":40,"category":"Verbs","title":"Group 1 conjugation","pattern":"U-row verb endings","meaning":"Group 1 verb conjugation","explanation":"U-row verb endings expresses group 1 verb conjugation. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"書く→書きます; 読む→読みます","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"毎日、本を読みます。","romaji":"Mainichi hon o yomimasu.","meaning":"I read a book every day."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction 書く→書きます; 読む→読みます; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-40-meaning","prompt":"What does “U-row verb endings” mean?","options":["Group 1 verb conjugation","Do / will do politely","Do not / will not","Did"],"answer":"Group 1 verb conjugation","explanation":"U-row verb endings expresses group 1 verb conjugation. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-40-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Group 1 conjugation”.","options":["Verb stem + ます","Verb stem + ません","Verb stem + ました","書く→書きます; 読む→読みます"],"answer":"書く→書きます; 読む→読みます","explanation":"U-row verb endings expresses group 1 verb conjugation. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-40-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Group 1 conjugation”?","options":["コーヒーを飲みません。","昨日、本を読みました。","毎日、本を読みます。","毎朝パンを食べます。"],"answer":"毎日、本を読みます。","explanation":"毎日、本を読みます。 (Mainichi hon o yomimasu.) means “I read a book every day.”."},{"id":"n5-40-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 毎日、本を読みます。","options":["I read a book yesterday.","I read a book every day.","I eat bread every morning.","I do not drink coffee."],"answer":"I read a book every day.","explanation":"毎日、本を読みます。 (Mainichi hon o yomimasu.) means “I read a book every day.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":41,"category":"Verbs","title":"Group 2 conjugation","pattern":"Remove る + ending","meaning":"Group 2 verb conjugation","explanation":"Remove る + ending expresses group 2 verb conjugation. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"食べる→食べます; 見る→見ます","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"毎朝パンを食べます。","romaji":"Maiasa pan o tabemasu.","meaning":"I eat bread every morning."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction 食べる→食べます; 見る→見ます; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-41-meaning","prompt":"What does “Remove る + ending” mean?","options":["Do / will do politely","Do not / will not","Did","Group 2 verb conjugation"],"answer":"Group 2 verb conjugation","explanation":"Remove る + ending expresses group 2 verb conjugation. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-41-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Group 2 conjugation”.","options":["Verb stem + ません","Verb stem + ました","食べる→食べます; 見る→見ます","Verb stem + ます"],"answer":"食べる→食べます; 見る→見ます","explanation":"Remove る + ending expresses group 2 verb conjugation. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-41-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Group 2 conjugation”?","options":["昨日は勉強しませんでした。","毎朝パンを食べます。","コーヒーを飲みません。","昨日、本を読みました。"],"answer":"毎朝パンを食べます。","explanation":"毎朝パンを食べます。 (Maiasa pan o tabemasu.) means “I eat bread every morning.”."},{"id":"n5-41-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 毎朝パンを食べます。","options":["I eat bread every morning.","I do not drink coffee.","I read a book yesterday.","I did not study yesterday."],"answer":"I eat bread every morning.","explanation":"毎朝パンを食べます。 (Maiasa pan o tabemasu.) means “I eat bread every morning.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":42,"category":"Verbs","title":"Irregular verbs","pattern":"する / 来る","meaning":"Irregular verb conjugation","explanation":"する / 来る expresses irregular verb conjugation. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"する→します; 来る→来ます","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"毎日勉強します。","romaji":"Mainichi benkyou shimasu.","meaning":"I study every day."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction する→します; 来る→来ます; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-42-meaning","prompt":"What does “する / 来る” mean?","options":["Do not / will not","Did","Irregular verb conjugation","Do / will do politely"],"answer":"Irregular verb conjugation","explanation":"する / 来る expresses irregular verb conjugation. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-42-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Irregular verbs”.","options":["Verb stem + ました","する→します; 来る→来ます","Verb stem + ます","Verb stem + ません"],"answer":"する→します; 来る→来ます","explanation":"する / 来る expresses irregular verb conjugation. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-42-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Irregular verbs”?","options":["毎日勉強します。","毎朝パンを食べます。","コーヒーを飲みません。","昨日、本を読みました。"],"answer":"毎日勉強します。","explanation":"毎日勉強します。 (Mainichi benkyou shimasu.) means “I study every day.”."},{"id":"n5-42-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 毎日勉強します。","options":["I eat bread every morning.","I do not drink coffee.","I read a book yesterday.","I study every day."],"answer":"I study every day.","explanation":"毎日勉強します。 (Mainichi benkyou shimasu.) means “I study every day.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":43,"category":"Verbs","title":"Te-form","pattern":"Verb て-form","meaning":"Connect actions / build requests","explanation":"Verb て-form expresses connect actions / build requests. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Group 2 remove る + て; する→して; 来る→来て","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"朝ご飯を食べて学校へ行きます。","romaji":"Asagohan o tabete gakkou e ikimasu.","meaning":"I eat breakfast and go to school."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Group 2 remove る + て; する→して; 来る→来て; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-43-meaning","prompt":"What does “Verb て-form” mean?","options":["Did","Connect actions / build requests","Do / will do politely","Do not / will not"],"answer":"Connect actions / build requests","explanation":"Verb て-form expresses connect actions / build requests. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-43-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Te-form”.","options":["Group 2 remove る + て; する→して; 来る→来て","Verb stem + ます","Verb stem + ません","Verb stem + ました"],"answer":"Group 2 remove る + て; する→して; 来る→来て","explanation":"Verb て-form expresses connect actions / build requests. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-43-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Te-form”?","options":["毎朝パンを食べます。","コーヒーを飲みません。","昨日、本を読みました。","朝ご飯を食べて学校へ行きます。"],"answer":"朝ご飯を食べて学校へ行きます。","explanation":"朝ご飯を食べて学校へ行きます。 (Asagohan o tabete gakkou e ikimasu.) means “I eat breakfast and go to school.”."},{"id":"n5-43-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 朝ご飯を食べて学校へ行きます。","options":["I do not drink coffee.","I read a book yesterday.","I eat breakfast and go to school.","I eat bread every morning."],"answer":"I eat breakfast and go to school.","explanation":"朝ご飯を食べて学校へ行きます。 (Asagohan o tabete gakkou e ikimasu.) means “I eat breakfast and go to school.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":44,"category":"Verbs","title":"Negative ない-form","pattern":"Verb ない-form","meaning":"Do not (plain)","explanation":"Verb ない-form expresses do not (plain). Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Group 1 u→a + ない; Group 2 remove る + ない","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"今日は学校へ行かない。","romaji":"Kyou wa gakkou e ikanai.","meaning":"I am not going to school today."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Group 1 u→a + ない; Group 2 rem