 / will do politely","Do not / will not","Did","Did (plain)"],"answer":"Did (plain)","explanation":"Verb た-form expresses did (plain). Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-45-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Past た-form”.","options":["Verb stem + ません","Verb stem + ました","Te-form て→た; で→だ","Verb stem + ます"],"answer":"Te-form て→た; で→だ","explanation":"Verb た-form expresses did (plain). Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-45-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Past た-form”?","options":["昨日、本を読みました。","昨日、映画を見た。","毎朝パンを食べます。","コーヒーを飲みません。"],"answer":"昨日、映画を見た。","explanation":"昨日、映画を見た。 (Kinou eiga o mita.) means “I watched a movie yesterday.”."},{"id":"n5-45-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 昨日、映画を見た。","options":["I watched a movie yesterday.","I eat bread every morning.","I do not drink coffee.","I read a book yesterday."],"answer":"I watched a movie yesterday.","explanation":"昨日、映画を見た。 (Kinou eiga o mita.) means “I watched a movie yesterday.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":46,"category":"Verbs","title":"Polite request てください","pattern":"Verb て-form + ください","meaning":"Please do","explanation":"Verb て-form + ください expresses please do. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Verb て-form + ください","difficulty":"Core","examples":[{"japanese":"ここに名前を書いてください。","romaji":"Koko ni namae o kaite kudasai.","meaning":"Please write your name here."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Verb て-form + ください; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-46-meaning","prompt":"What does “Verb て-form + ください” mean?","options":["Do not / will not","Did","Please do","Do / will do politely"],"answer":"Please do","explanation":"Verb て-form + ください expresses please do. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"