 action","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"三時間勉強しました。","romaji":"San-jikan benkyou shimashita.","meaning":"I studied for three hours."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Duration + action; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-82-meaning","prompt":"What does “Duration + verb” mean?","options":["After doing","When / at the time","For a duration","Before doing"],"answer":"For a duration","explanation":"Duration + verb expresses for a duration. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-82-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Duration”.","options":["Plain form + とき","Duration + action","Verb dictionary + まえに","Verb た-form + あとで"],"answer":"Duration + action","explanation":"Duration + verb expresses for a duration. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-82-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Duration”?","options":["三時間勉強しました。","寝るまえに本を読みます。","宿題をしたあとでテレビを見ます。","日本へ行くときカメラを買います。"],"answer":"三時間勉強しました。","explanation":"三時間勉強しました。 (San-jikan benkyou shimashita.) means “I studied for three hours.”."},{"id":"n5-82-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 三時間勉強しました。","options":["I read before sleeping.","I watch TV after doing homework.","When I go to Japan, I will buy a camera.","I studied for three hours."],"answer":"I studied for three hours.","explanation":"三時間勉強しました。 (San-jikan benkyou shimashita.) means “I studied for three hours.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":83,"category":"Time","title":"Specific day/date に","pattern":"Day / date + に","meaning":"On a specific day","explanation":"Day / date + に expresses on a specific day. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Day / date + に + event","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"日曜日に友達に会います。","romaji":"Nichiyoubi ni tomodachi ni aimasu.","meaning":"I will m