 / 四人","Number + 歳 + です","Number + 分 + に"],"answer":"Number + 分 + に","explanation":"Number + 分 expresses minutes on a clock. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-88-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Clock minutes 分”?","options":["教室に学生が三人います。","妹は十歳です。","駅まで十分かかります。","りんごを三つ買いました。"],"answer":"駅まで十分かかります。","explanation":"駅まで十分かかります。 (Eki made juppun kakarimasu.) means “It takes ten minutes to the station.”."},{"id":"n5-88-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 駅まで十分かかります。","options":["My younger sister is ten.","It takes ten minutes to the station.","I bought three apples.","There are three students in the classroom."],"answer":"It takes ten minutes to the station.","explanation":"駅まで十分かかります。 (Eki made juppun kakarimasu.) means “It takes ten minutes to the station.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":89,"category":"Counting","title":"Times counter 回","pattern":"Number + 回","meaning":"Number of times","explanation":"Number + 回 expresses number of times. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Number + 回 + action","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"週に三回運動します。","romaji":"Shuu ni san-kai undou shimasu.","meaning":"I exercise three times a week."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Number + 回 + action; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-89-meaning","prompt":"What does “Number + 回” mean?","options":["Count general objects","Number of people","Age in years","Number of times"],"answer":"Number of times","explanation":"Number + 回 expresses number of times. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-89-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Times counter 回”.","options":["ひとり / ふたり / 三人 / 四人","Number + 歳 + です","Number + 回 + action","ひとつ / ふたつ / みっつ ..."],"answer":"Number + 回 + action","explanation":"Number + 回 expresses number of times. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-89-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Times counter 回”?","options":["妹は十歳です。","週に三回運動します。","りんごを三つ買いました。","教室に学生が三人います。"],"answer":"週に三回運動します。","explanation":"週に三回運動します。 (Shuu ni san-kai undou shimasu.) means “I exercise three times a week.”."},{"id":"n5-89-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 週に三回運動します。","options":["I exercise three times a week.","I bought three apples.","There are three students in the classroom.","My younger sister is ten."],"answer":"I exercise three times a week.","explanation":"週に三回運動します。 (Shuu ni san-kai undou shimasu.) means “I exercise three times a week.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":90,"category":"Quantity","title":"About ぐらい","pattern":"Quantity + ぐらい","meaning":"About / approximately","explanation":"Quantity + ぐらい expresses about / approximately. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Quantity + ぐらい","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"一時間ぐらい勉強します。","romaji":"Ichi-jikan gurai benkyou shimasu.","meaning":"I study for about one hour."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Quantity + ぐらい; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-90-meaning","prompt":"What does “Quantity + ぐらい” mean?","options":["A is not B","A is not B (formal)","About / approximately","A is B"],"answer":"About / approximately","explanation":"Quantity + ぐらい expresses about / approximately. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-90-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “About ぐらい”.","options":["Noun + は + Noun + ではありません","Quantity + ぐらい","Noun + は + Noun + です","Noun + は + Noun + じゃありません"],"answer":"Quantity + ぐらい","explanation":"Quantity + ぐらい expresses about / approximately. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-90-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “About ぐらい”?","options":["一時間ぐらい勉強します。","私は学生です。","私は医者じゃありません。","これは問題ではありません。"],"answer":"一時間ぐらい勉強します。","explanation":"一時間ぐらい勉強します。 (Ichi-jikan gurai benkyou shimasu.) means “I study for about one hour.”."},{"id":"n5-90-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 一時間ぐらい勉強します。","options":["I am a student.","I am not a doctor.","This is not a problem.","I study for about one hour."],"answer":"I study for about one hour.","explanation":"一時間ぐらい勉強します。 (Ichi-jikan gurai benkyou shimasu.) means “I study for about one hour.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":91,"category":"Comparison","title":"More than より","pattern":"A は B より + adjective","meaning":"A is more ... than B","explanation":"A は B より + adjective expresses a is more ... than b. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"A は B より + adjective","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"東京は大阪より大きいです。","romaji":"Toukyou wa Oosaka yori ookii desu.","meaning":"Tokyo is bigger than Osaka."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction A は B より + adjective; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-91-meaning","prompt":"What does “A は B より + adjective” mean?","options":["A is not B (formal)","A is more ... than B","A is B","A is not B"],"answer":"A is more ... than B","explanation":"A は B より + adjective expresses a is more ... than b. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-91-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “More than より”.","options":["A は B より + adjective","Noun + は + Noun + です","Noun + は + Noun + じゃありません","Noun + は + Noun + ではありません"],"answer":"A は B より + adjective","explanation":"A は B より + adjective expresses a is more ... than b. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-91-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “More than より”?","options":["私は学生です。","私は医者じゃありません。","これは問題ではありません。","東京は大阪より大きいです。"],"answer":"東京は大阪より大きいです。","explanation":"東京は大阪より大きいです。 (Toukyou wa Oosaka yori ookii desu.) means “Tokyo is bigger than Osaka.”."},{"id":"n5-91-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 東京は大阪より大きいです。","options":["I am not a doctor.","This is not a problem.","Tokyo is bigger than Osaka.","I am a student."],"answer":"Tokyo is bigger than Osaka.","explanation":"東京は大阪より大きいです。 (Toukyou wa Oosaka yori ookii desu.) means “Tokyo is bigger than Osaka.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":92,"category":"Comparison","title":"Prefer のほうが","pattern":"A のほうが B より ...","meaning":"A is more ... than B","explanation":"A のほうが B より ... expresses a is more ... than b. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"A のほうが B より + adjective","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"電車のほうがバスより速いです。","romaji":"Densha no hou ga basu yori hayai desu.","meaning":"Trains are faster than buses."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction A のほうが B より + adjective; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-92-meaning","prompt":"What does “A のほうが B より ...” mean?","options":["A is more ... than B","A is B","A is not B","A is not B (formal)"],"answer":"A is more ... than B","explanation":"A のほうが B より ... expresses a is more ... than b. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-92-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Prefer のほうが”.","options":["Noun + は + Noun + です","Noun + は + Noun + じゃありません","Noun + は + Noun + ではありません","A のほうが B より + adjective"],"answer":"A のほうが B より + adjective","explanation":"A のほうが B より ... expresses a is more ... than b. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-92-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Prefer のほうが”?","options":["私は医者じゃありません。","これは問題ではありません。","電車のほうがバスより速いです。","私は学生です。"],"answer":"電車のほうがバスより速いです。","explanation":"電車のほうがバスより速いです。 (Densha no hou ga basu yori hayai desu.) means “Trains are faster than buses.”."},{"id":"n5-92-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 電車のほうがバスより速いです。","options":["This is not a problem.","Trains are faster than buses.","I am a student.","I am not a doctor."],"answer":"Trains are faster than buses.","explanation":"電車のほうがバスより速いです。 (Densha no hou ga basu yori hayai desu.) means “Trains are faster than buses.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":93,"category":"Comparison","title":"The most いちばん","pattern":"いちばん + adjective","meaning":"The most","explanation":"いちばん + adjective expresses the most. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Group で + item が + いちばん + adjective","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"果物の中でりんごがいちばん好きです。","romaji":"Kudamono no naka de ringo ga ichiban suki desu.","meaning":"Among fruits, I like apples the most."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Group で + item が + いちばん + adjective; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-93-meaning","prompt":"What does “いちばん + adjective” mean?","options":["A is B","A is not B","A is not B (formal)","The most"],"answer":"The most","explanation":"いちばん + adjective expresses the most. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-93-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “The most いちばん”.","options":["Noun + は + Noun + じゃありません","Noun + は + Noun + ではありません","Group で + item が + いちばん + adjective","Noun + は + Noun + です"],"answer":"Group で + item が + いちばん + adjective","explanation":"いちばん + adjective expresses the most. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-93-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “The most いちばん”?","options":["これは問題ではありません。","果物の中でりんごがいちばん好きです。","私は学生です。","私は医者じゃありません。"],"answer":"果物の中でりんごがいちばん好きです。","explanation":"果物の中でりんごがいちばん好きです。 (Kudamono no naka de ringo ga ichiban suki desu.) means “Among fruits, I like apples the most.”."},{"id":"n5-93-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 果物の中でりんごがいちばん好きです。","options":["Among fruits, I like apples the most.","I am a student.","I am not a doctor.","This is not a problem."],"answer":"Among fruits, I like apples the most.","explanation":"果物の中でりんごがいちばん好きです。 (Kudamono no naka de ringo ga ichiban suki desu.) means “Among fruits, I like apples the most.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":94,"category":"Reason","title":"Because から","pattern":"Reason clause + から","meaning":"Because","explanation":"Reason clause + から expresses because. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Reason + から + result","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"雨が降っていますから出かけません。","romaji":"Ame ga futte imasu kara dekakemasen.","meaning":"Because it is raining, I will not go out."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Reason + から + result; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-94-meaning","prompt":"What does “Reason clause + から” mean?","options":["A is not B","A is not B (formal)","Because","A is B"],"answer":"Because","explanation":"Reason clause + から expresses because. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-94-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “Because から”.","options":["Noun + は + Noun + ではありません","Reason + から + result","Noun + は + Noun + です","Noun + は + Noun + じゃありません"],"answer":"Reason + から + result","explanation":"Reason clause + から expresses because. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-94-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “Because から”?","options":["雨が降っていますから出かけません。","私は学生です。","私は医者じゃありません。","これは問題ではありません。"],"answer":"雨が降っていますから出かけません。","explanation":"雨が降っていますから出かけません。 (Ame ga futte imasu kara dekakemasen.) means “Because it is raining, I will not go out.”."},{"id":"n5-94-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: 雨が降っていますから出かけません。","options":["I am a student.","I am not a doctor.","This is not a problem.","Because it is raining, I will not go out."],"answer":"Because it is raining, I will not go out.","explanation":"雨が降っていますから出かけません。 (Ame ga futte imasu kara dekakemasen.) means “Because it is raining, I will not go out.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":95,"category":"Connection","title":"But でも","pattern":"Sentence start + でも","meaning":"But / however","explanation":"Sentence start + でも expresses but / however. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Sentence. でも + contrasting sentence","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"この店は高いです。でも、おいしいです。","romaji":"Kono mise wa takai desu. Demo, oishii desu.","meaning":"This shop is expensive. But it is delicious."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Sentence. でも + contrasting sentence; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-95-meaning","prompt":"What does “Sentence start + でも” mean?","options":["A is not B (formal)","But / however","A is B","A is not B"],"answer":"But / however","explanation":"Sentence start + でも expresses but / however. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-95-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “But でも”.","options":["Sentence. でも + contrasting sentence","Noun + は + Noun + です","Noun + は + Noun + じゃありません","Noun + は + Noun + ではありません"],"answer":"Sentence. でも + contrasting sentence","explanation":"Sentence start + でも expresses but / however. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-95-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “But でも”?","options":["私は学生です。","私は医者じゃありません。","これは問題ではありません。","この店は高いです。でも、おいしいです。"],"answer":"この店は高いです。でも、おいしいです。","explanation":"この店は高いです。でも、おいしいです。 (Kono mise wa takai desu. Demo, oishii desu.) means “This shop is expensive. But it is delicious.”."},{"id":"n5-95-translation","prompt":"Choose the meaning of: この店は高いです。でも、おいしいです。","options":["I am not a doctor.","This is not a problem.","This shop is expensive. But it is delicious.","I am a student."],"answer":"This shop is expensive. But it is delicious.","explanation":"この店は高いです。でも、おいしいです。 (Kono mise wa takai desu. Demo, oishii desu.) means “This shop is expensive. But it is delicious.”."}]},{"jlpt_level":"N5","sort_order":96,"category":"Connection","title":"And then そして","pattern":"Sentence + そして + sentence","meaning":"And then / moreover","explanation":"Sentence + そして + sentence expresses and then / moreover. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context.","formation":"Sentence + そして + sentence","difficulty":"Challenge","examples":[{"japanese":"朝ご飯を食べました。そして学校へ行きました。","romaji":"Asagohan o tabemashita. Soshite gakkou e ikimashita.","meaning":"I ate breakfast. Then I went to school."}],"common_mistakes":["Use the exact construction Sentence + そして + sentence; do not replace it with a similar-looking pattern."],"practice_questions":[{"id":"n5-96-meaning","prompt":"What does “Sentence + そして + sentence” mean?","options":["And then / moreover","A is B","A is not B","A is not B (formal)"],"answer":"And then / moreover","explanation":"Sentence + そして + sentence expresses and then / moreover. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-96-formation","prompt":"Choose the correct formation for “And then そして”.","options":["Noun + は + Noun + です","Noun + は + Noun + じゃありません","Noun + は + Noun + ではありません","Sentence + そして + sentence"],"answer":"Sentence + そして + sentence","explanation":"Sentence + そして + sentence expresses and then / moreover. Identify the role of each phrase, then apply the formation rule in context."},{"id":"n5-96-example","prompt":"Which sentence illustrates “And then そして”?","options":["私は医者じゃありません。","これは問題